    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T13:07:53Z",
    "body": "the cancel-and-renavigate could be intended for libraries but I thought it would have been powerful to be able to intercept the redirect happening from a navigation without an abstraction layer created by libs.\nI think the comment at https://github.com/WICG/navigation-api/issues/5#issuecomment-2684388491 is related but can be independent from above:\n\n> In SPA routers, it would be useful to write state and info in each navigation. Right now these properties are only writable if they exist but that's only if doing navigation.navigate('...', { state: {}, info: {} }). Adding transitive info is particularly useful for users who want to access or augment the navigation cycle at different points. e.g. collecting fetching calls based on the pages we are navigating to without calling them and verifying authenticated access to a page (this can happen in parallel in the same pass), then in a different interception, call the fetches. This allows routers to let users use the Navigation API to customize the navigation, it makes it easy for routers to let their users customize things",
